      "text": "San Miguel de Allende – Dolores Hidalgo – Guanajuato"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2dac387926637cb09fa93ae9a1f6df4b18851c55ee92550971ed6cd1c8056a39",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-o0ph8fryncjmw9u91va",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, leave for Dolores Hidalgo.\n\nThe town is closely associated with the start of Mexico’s struggle for independence. In 1810, the priest Miguel Hidalgo made his famous call to rise up against Spanish rule here. Today, you can see colonial buildings, markets and artisans’ workshops. The town produces traditional Talavera pottery and is also known for its ice cream.\n\nContinue to Guanajuato. On your tour, visit the famous Alley of the Kiss, the setting of a romantic legend about forbidden love.\n\nAnother stop is the neoclassical Juárez Theatre. Then see the Basilica of Our Lady of Guanajuato with its Baroque façade and the Plaza de la Paz, a central square with cafés and shops.\n\nThe city is known for its colourful hillside houses, narrow streets and underground roads. In your free time, you can explore more of the historic centre."
    },
